  "implemented": [
    "A private explicit version-three physical catalog retains seven concrete native file families, including separately tagged local snapshots and flat local provenance. Every older reader, wire/schema/default meaning and public-root export remains unchanged.",
    "Fresh read-only native policy is independently selected per local file, with exact family, catalog ID and original identity. Graph policies retain their separate delivery meaning; imported data cannot select factories or reuse a writer grant.",
    "Actual canonical readers, archive owners, database connections and cooperative leases conserve the complete immutable file table. Distinct V3 stores are absent-only and cold re-admit every file; occupied, old-schema and acknowledged missing-file destinations refuse without overwrite or reconstruction.",
    "Incoming local source captures bind the actual admitted archive handle. Reopening requires fresh genuine captures; local comments stay unbound and every omitted historical copy stays unresolved.",
    "Final native/input witnesses run after policy and wrapper callbacks, including the catalog parent final callback. They check actual registry ownership and native lane epochs, admitted file lifetime and local source/journal/storage/version stamps without invoking another permission/factory callback.",
    "The final native witness is not complete legacy retained-store or provider epoch coverage, writer/upload custody, disposition or authenticated activation. None of those obligations is replaced by a checked data flag."
  ],
